351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 169 0 R
/T (Conclusion Analysis: The high accuracy is a positive sign, but given the imbalanced nature of landslide detection \(landslide areas are usually small\), the F1-Score provides a more reliable assessment. An F1-Score of 0.7106 demonstrates a strong capability in balancing precision and recall. While precision is higher \(0.7859\), suggesting fewer false positives, the recall \(0.6523\) indicates some actual landslide areas might still be missed. This trade-off is common and points to areas for future optimization, possibly by further addressing class imbalance or exploring architectural enhancements.)
